			"date": "2024-01-29T14:35:40.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.cc/@jgarber\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jgarber</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> And from that neck of the woods, Brid.gy is definitely looking into (might already have?) some of that functionality. I know BlueSky bridges are being worked on their.</p><p>Twitter is a bigger issue because they killed the APIs those services used. Maybe some kind of Zapier or Buffer integration?</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
