			"url": "https://mastodon.cc/@jgarber/111840367978410952",
			"author": {
				"name": "Jason Garber",
				"url": "https://mastodon.cc/@jgarber",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/286/956/268/376/133/original/c0aca1e4fd362889.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-01-29T17:16:23.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Ah! I get you. Okay, yeah, that’s different.</p><p>Things you’d probably need at a minimum:</p><p>• something linking the “same” post from Networks A…n, and/or<br>• something linking the same user’s profiles from Networks A…n, and<br>• associations between your profiles on all those networks, and<br>• the means to boost those posts across all those networks by any number of means.</p><p>🤔</p><p>Maybe doable? Seems fraught, though.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111840372028633607",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.design/@DavidDarnes/111840371988744269",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dave 🧱 :cursor_pointer:",
